---
import DocumentationLayout from '../../layouts/DocumentationLayout.astro';
import ImplementationSupport from './ImplementationSupport.astro';
import PreviewControls from './PreviewControls.astro';
import OTPVerificationPreview from './OTPVerificationPreview.astro';
import {OTPVerificationBlock} from '../dmf-ui/blocks';
import {CodeSnippet} from '../dmf-ui/code-block';
import {blocks} from '../../data/blocks';
import catalog from '../../../contracts/catalog.json';
const block=blocks.find(b=>b.slug==='otp-verification')!,record=catalog.blocks.find(b=>b.slug===block.slug)!,react=catalog.react.blocks.find(b=>b.name===block.title)!;
---
<DocumentationLayout title={block.title} description={block.description} section="blocks" crumbs={[{name:'Blocks',href:'/blocks/'},{name:block.title}]} toc={[{id:'entry',title:'OTP entry contract'},{id:'preview',title:'Preview'},{id:'usage',title:'Usage and API'},{id:'states',title:'States'},{id:'ownership',title:'Host responsibilities'}]}>
<h1 class="docs-block-title">{block.title}</h1><p class="docs-lead">{block.description}</p><ImplementationSupport slug={block.slug} kind="block"/>
<section id="entry" class="docs-section docs-prose"><h2>OTP entry contract</h2><p>One existing Input renders a text field with inputmode=numeric, autocomplete=one-time-code and explicit ASCII digit length constraints. The default is six digits; codeLength accepts integers from 1 through 12. Leading zeroes remain text. Whole-code paste and selection use the native input. Paste is not intercepted or normalized; spaces, separators and non-ASCII characters do not satisfy the pattern. Hosts needing other formats should compose the existing Input.</p><p>Keyboard editing, Tab, Backspace and Enter retain native behavior. Filling the field never auto-submits or advances focus. dir=ltr keeps ASCII code order within an RTL layout. No initial-code prop, segmented digit widget, WebOTP retrieval or code-generation API is introduced. Actual OS/device autofill remains a manual acceptance check.</p></section>
<section id="preview" class="docs-section"><h2>Live preview</h2><PreviewControls/><OTPVerificationPreview/></section>
<section id="usage" class="docs-section docs-prose"><h2>Astro and React usage</h2><p>Import shared styles once inside .dmf-ui. Both actions are real host-owned POST destinations. Unverified is the default; ready is presentation of a host-issued challenge, never authorization.</p><CodeSnippet code={block.usage} language="astro" title="Astro OTP form" wrap/><CodeSnippet code={`import {OTPVerificationBlock} from '@dmf-ui/react';\nimport '@dmf-ui/react/styles.css';\n\n<OTPVerificationBlock id="account-code" action="/account/verify"\n  challengeState="ready" resendAction="/account/resend" />`} language="tsx" title="React OTP form" wrap/><p>The wrapper groups two sibling native forms. id/action, ref, native attributes, class/style and onSubmit apply to the primary form. React onResendSubmit and resendFormRef target the optional sibling resend form. fields and resendFields correspond to Astro fields and resend-fields slots; provide separate CSRF/context fields for each action. footer belongs to the primary Card; default children follow both forms. Never nest forms. Multiple instances need distinct IDs, titles and resend labels.</p><p>The resend form contains no code control. Capture values before setting pending because disabled fieldsets are omitted from FormData. Neither the code nor server challenge state is stored internally; native reset clears entry only. Challenge changes that remove the input should focus the stable -status paragraph after an explicit transition, without initial autofocus.</p><CodeSnippet code={record.declaration} language="ts" title="Astro Props" wrap/><CodeSnippet code={react.types[0].declaration} language="ts" title="React Props" wrap/><h3>Authored defaults</h3><div class="docs-table-scroll"><table class="docs-options"><thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody>{Object.entries(record.defaults).map(([key,value])=><tr><td><code>{key}</code></td><td><code>{String(value)}</code></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>
<section id="states" class="docs-section docs-prose"><h2>Challenge, verification and resend states</h2><p>unverified, expired, locked and complete omit code/extension fields. Resend is available only in ready or expired states when a resendAction exists and the host permits it. pending and resendPending freeze both fieldsets; disabled makes both unavailable. submitDisabled affects verification only; resendDisabled affects resend only. The host owns cooldown text through resendHelp/resendStatus and disabled state. No countdown, retry limit, attempt counter or request is created by the library.</p>{(['unverified','expired','locked'] as const).map(state=><OTPVerificationBlock id={`otp-${state}`} title={`OTP ${state} example`} action="/account/verify" challengeState={state}/>)}<OTPVerificationBlock id="otp-errors" title="OTP validation example" action="/account/verify" challengeState="ready" disabled error="Illustrative host verification error." fieldErrors={{code:'Review the code with your account service.'}}/><OTPVerificationBlock id="otp-pending" title="OTP pending example" action="/account/verify" challengeState="ready" pending/><OTPVerificationBlock id="otp-resend-pending" title="OTP resend pending example" action="/account/verify" challengeState="ready" resendAction="/account/resend" resendLabel="Request code for pending specimen" resendPending/><OTPVerificationBlock id="otp-complete" title="OTP completion example" action="/account/verify" complete/></section>
<section id="ownership" class="docs-section docs-prose"><h2>Ownership and acceptance</h2><p>{block.limitations}</p><p>Code length/pattern and disabled flags are UI constraints, not authentication security or rate limiting. The server verifies challenge binding, attempts, expiry and single-use on every request, and controls delivery, replacement of old codes, CSRF protection and sessions. No channel, destination or factor-strength claim is implied. Example buttons change local UI state only.</p><p>Natural sizing, logical spacing and the shared 28rem form bound support narrow containers. New pending labels use the established flow layout. Nova/Neutral defaults and brand fills are unchanged. White CB/HUI primary text retains the approximately 2.57:1/4.29:1 normal-text exceptions; these are not AA passes. No submit-variant prop is exposed. Safari, Firefox, physical keyboards/devices, real autofill and spoken readers remain separately unverified.</p><p><a href="/examples/authentication/">Authentication journey</a> · <a href="/docs/authentication/">Workflow pattern</a> · <a href="/blocks/reset-password/">ResetPasswordBlock</a> · <a href="/docs/implementation-paths/">Adapter setup</a></p></section>
</DocumentationLayout>
